                "quoted_status_profile_id": null,
                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 59,
                "retweet_count": 9,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "In communities across the State of Maine, nurse practitioners and physician assistants deliver high-quality and compassionate care that so many Mainers rely on. But under current law, they aren\u2019t allowed to certify or oversee treatment for federal employees who are injured on the job, even when they are the primary health care provider for those federal employees.\n\nThis week, I introduced bipartisan legislation to ensure injured federal workers can receive care from the trusted NPs and PAs who already serve as primary providers at many of Maine\u2019s health care facilities, especially in rural areas, where they are often the only available providers for miles.\n\nBy allowing injured federal workers to be treated by these highly skilled and experienced professionals, we can reduce patient travel times, shorten wait lists for care, and break down barriers to access care.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
